{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba PAID-DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The paid whole-window comparison of poc-v120 against fresh controls: design, version 2 (D699, D705, D706; for council review)\n     2\t\n     3\tVersion 1 was reviewed in council R round 22 (`codex-r22.md`, part B NOT READY: four changes); each is answered below (§7).\n     4\t\n     5\t## 0. What it decides, and what it can reach\n     6\t\n     7\tIt decides whether linking (poc-v120: Jev's link questions version 2; judging-v8's fuller dependency block) makes the linked number\n     8\tquestions' judgements agree over the release window without harm elsewhere: the evidence for Alex's choice whether the linking version\n     9\treplaces poc-v118 (D699). It is paired on old-2's trajectory (DESIGN.md §1): every request byte-equal to one old-2 sent is answered with\n    10\told-2's answer; only the readers' judgements are bought.\n    11\t\n    12\t**The attainable verdict ($0):** Data Center FY2027 above total revenue FY2027 (`contradictions.py`, calendar dates 07-01..09-20,\n    13\tparser second version, before hand reading): old-1 11 days of 77, old-2 56 of 73, old-3 1 of 33 (that one a misparse,\n    14\t`parser-validation.md`). The class occurs and varies widely between draws; old-2's stored path is an extreme and not a fair control.\n    15\tA linked sequence that reconciles would show near zero; only fresh controls can serve as the baseline.\n    16\t\n    17\t## 1. Arms (paired by draw n = 1, 2, 3)\n    18\t\n    19\t- **linked-n:** poc-v120 from an empty store on its own copy of old-2's archive. Its link jobs are answered only by probe draw n's\n    20\t  answers, matched by request hash (`window_test.probe_answers`; any other link job stops the sequence before a purchase), so its links\n    21\t  are probe draw n's proposals, now written. Readers in all three draws: v9 (Data Center FY2027, reads v14), v14 (total revenue FY2027,\n    22\t  reads v8), v16 (total CPU FY2027, reads v14), v21 (revenue growth FY2027, reads v16, and v9 in draws 2 and 3).\n    23\t- **control-n:** poc-v118 from an empty store on its own copy of old-2's archive, its readers' old judgements retired as below.\n    24\t- **Fresh judgements, delimited by date (round 22):** a reader's link is written by an article of day D_R (v9, v14: 07-10, seq 148;\n    25\t  v16: seq 265's day; v21: seq 534's day); its first affected judgement is its first judgement on a day at or after D_R (old-2: seq 167,\n    26\t  274, 542). Every judgement of a reader on a day at or after D_R must be a fresh answer in both arms: in linked-n because its request\n    27\t  carries the dependency block, in control-n because the old request family is retired. The old family of a reader is identified by\n    28\t  reader and judgement day: every archive judge row of that reader (accepted answers, first attempts the stored run refused, and their\n    29\t  retries) whose judgement day is at or after D_R; archive rows carry no day, so a row is assigned to a day through old-2's\n    30\t  `judgements` table (accepted rows) and through its request text (the refused first attempts, whose request equals the retry's before\n    31\t  the correction lines). Every retired row is listed before the send and checked against old-2's judgements by reader and day.\n    32\t- **old-2's stored path:** a labelled historical baseline, outside the fresh-control figures.\n    33\t- All six sequences run at once, one paid call at a time within each (July's latch, round 22), one shared reservation ledger at the\n    34\t  ceiling Alex names.\n    35\t\n    36\t## 2. Harness rules (July's, `dependency-design/july_test.py`, extended to the window)\n    37\t\n    38\t- Harness-only marker, the store lock, never resumed; any stop is final and makes the comparison inconclusive.\n    39\t- **Allow-list before the budget transport, per sequence, under July's latch** (admission and the inner call under one lock; the first\n    40\t  refusal closes the sequence): a linked sequence may buy only judge requests of its readers on days at or after their D_R; a control\n    41\t  only the retired readers' judge requests on those days; a link job only from the probe draw. Any other request that misses the archive\n    42\t  stops the sequence (round 22 found no legitimate non-reader change on this trajectory). The four answers old-2's own run refused are\n    43\t  given back once each for non-readers, as in the `neither` pass.\n    44\t- Settlement at published rates with cache writes at 1.25x; reservation from request size (D696).\n    45\t\n    46\t## 3. The $0 proofs before the send\n    47\t\n    48\t1. `v120-replay` (done): poc-v120 with each probe draw's own answers meets all 17 link jobs and ends equal to old-2.\n    49\t2. **Linked dry run per draw** (a fake judge answering readers with markers): committed links equal probe draw n's proposals; no link\n    50\t   job outside the probe; no circle correction; every non-reader judgement equal to old-2's by question and day in its request and its\n    51\t   substantive fields (rung, reasons, reference, implied outcome, cites); each reader fresh on every day at or after its D_R and only\n    52\t   then; each reader request shows, for each question it reads, the **latest accepted conclusion of that question available when the\n    53\t   request was built** (not only a same-day one: old-2's v14 has ten judgement days with no v8 judgement that day); the added days.\n    54\t3. **Control dry run per draw:** the retired rows listed and checked; only the retired readers reach the transport, on the right days;\n    55\t   every other judgement equal to old-2's by question and day.\n    56\t4. The stop paths and the latch race, on the window.\n    57\t5. Price from old-2's archived usage of the readers' days (round 22: 247 judgements, $0.872 a sequence) plus the dry runs' added days,\n    58\t   prompt growth from the dependency block, retries, and the live reservations, each shown apart.\n    59\t\n    60\t## 4. Reading rule (frozen before the send)\n    61\t\n    62\t**Unit:** a calendar date from 07-10 to 09-20 on which both v9 and v14 hold a conclusion in the sequence (each its last accepted\n    63\tjudgement on or before the date, carried forward). For each date, `contradictions.py` gives a lead class from the two annual forecasts\n    64\t(ranges kept: a definite contradiction only when Data Center's low end exceeds total revenue's high end; overlap; clear; ambiguous;\n    65\tunparsed). **Every distinct answer pair the parser flags definite or ambiguous, in all six sequences, is read by hand against both\n    66\tanswers and classed definite, overlap, clear or misparse; a random 15 unflagged distinct pairs per sequence are read for missed\n    67\tcontradictions, and all unflagged pairs of a sequence are read if one is found.** The hand class decides.\n    68\t\n    69\t**Coverage:** a sequence's dates with a hand-confirmed class over its dates with both conclusions; at least 80% in every sequence.\n    70\t\n    71\t**Primary line, P:** a sequence's rate = definite dates / covered dates.\n    72\t- **Pass:** coverage met in all six; every control at least 2 definite dates; each linked-n rate below its control-n rate (all three\n    73\t  pairs); and every harm line clean.\n    74\t- **Fail:** coverage and the control floor met and some pair not improved; or a harm line breached (confirmed material harm fails\n    75\t  whatever P shows).\n    76\t- **Inconclusive:** a stop or a refused reservation; coverage under 80% in a sequence; a control under 2 definite dates (the class did\n    77\t  not recur, as in July: \"not tested\").\n    78\t\n    79\t**Harm lines, H (each must hold for a pass):**\n    80\t- **H1, refusals and stops:** model refusals (a first attempt the code refused) per reader judgement, linked against its paired\n    81\t  control, reported with numerator and denominator; a linked rate above its control's by more than 5 percentage points with at least\n    82\t  3 more refusals is harm. An infrastructure stop (transport, budget, latch) is not a refusal: it makes the comparison inconclusive.\n    83\t- **H2:** every judgement outside the readers equal to old-2's by question and day, request and substantive fields (code).\n    84\t- **H3, sourcing:** a reader's reference or reasons that present a figure as the market's (consensus, guidance, \"the market\n    85\t  expects\") are traced to an outside statement of the right scope in the request **outside the dependency block and the previous\n    86\t  conclusion**; a market figure traced only to the system's own forecast is a grounding error. Keyword hits guide the reading; every\n    87\t  reader answer with a market claim in the seven fixed dates below, and every hit elsewhere, is read.\n    88\t- **H4, the CPU link (round 20, 22):** **every** post-link v14 answer in the three linked sequences is read against the exact CPU\n    89\t  conclusion it received and its paired control's v14 answer that day: its reference, forecast and arithmetic, whether or not v8 is\n    90\t  cited. Adding the whole CPU forecast to a company estimate that already includes it is harm; a supported increment over the amount\n    91\t  already included is not; an overlap the answer leaves unresolved is recorded.\n    92\t- **H5, arithmetic and sourcing (July's rule B):** v9 and v14 at seven fixed dates (07-12, 07-26, 08-09, 08-23, 09-06, 09-13, 09-20)\n    93\t  in all six sequences, by Claude and a blind reader: each assumption that sizes the result disclosed and supported, the arithmetic\n    94\t  following from stated inputs. A linked sequence with more material failures than its control, by at least 2, is harm.\n    95\t\n    96\t**Reported beside, not gating:** each link's relation, direction and sign (the weak CPU link disclosed); self-made references on the\n    97\treaders (`reference_census.py`'s three measures, the `unsourced` scan with the dependency block excluded); v14 linked against control\n    98\t(does the total move with the CPU link); v21's implied total against v9 and v14; linked-only judgement days.\n    99\t\n   100\t## 5. Cost (estimate; the ceiling is Alex's)\n   101\t\n   102\tReader judgements from their links, at published rates from old-2's archived usage: $0.872 a sequence (247 judgements, round 22).\n   103\tLinked sequences: about 19 added judgement days each (round 22's count on the fixed schedule; the dry runs give the exact count) and\n   104\tthe dependency block's prompt growth (about 10%): about $1.05. Three linked and three controls: about $5.8, plus retries and refusals\n   105\t(about 5%) and the live reservations (one judge call per sequence at once). Priced exactly from the dry runs before the ceiling\n   106\tquestion.\n   107\t\n   108\t## 6. Time\n   109\t\n   110\tOne paid call at a time per sequence: about 270–300 calls at about 30 seconds each, about 2.5 hours, the six sequences at once.\n   111\t\n   112\t## 7. Round 22 findings and where they are answered\n   113\t\n   114\t1. Fresh judgements by date, request families, latest available upstream conclusion, the stored refusals: §1 (fresh judgements), §2,\n   115\t   §3 items 2–3. 2. P on annual ranges, carry-forward, coverage, all three pairs, outcomes for every case, the parser validated on\n   116\t   flagged and unflagged stored answers: §4, `parser-validation.md`. 3. H4 on every post-link v14 answer; H3 traced outside the\n   117\t   dependency block; H5 with an effect on the verdict; per-link report; refusals with a denominator, stops apart: §4. 4. July's latch:\n   118\t   §1, §2, §6.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba contradictions.py; nl -ba parser-validation.md; wc -l parser-validation.txt; nl -ba parser-validation.txt | sed -n '1,140p'; ls -la | rg 'parser|PAID|cost|contradiction'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba contradictions.py; nl -ba parser-validation.md; wc -l parser-validation.txt; nl -ba parser-validation.txt | sed -n '1,140p'; ls -la | rg 'parser|PAID|cost|contradiction'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"The primary line P of the paid comparison (PAID-DESIGN.md §4): per store, for each calendar date from the link day to the window's\n     2\tend on which both the Data Center question and the total revenue question (FY2027) hold a conclusion, compare their annual forecasts.\n     3\t\n     4\tEach question's conclusion on a date is its last accepted judgement on or before that date (carried forward). Its annual forecast is\n     5\tan amount or range in its `implied_outcome` between $200B and $1,000B, chosen by `annual` (the last one followed by \"FY2027\", else one\n     6\topening the text, else the last one): a range (\"$400–410B\", \"$390 billion to $395 billion\") gives its low and high ends; a single\n     7\tamount gives both. A date is\n     8\t  definite:  the segment's low end exceeds the company's high end (the part above the whole whatever the range);\n     9\t  overlap:   the two ranges share some value without the part being wholly above (reported, not counted as a contradiction);\n    10\t  clear:     the segment's high end is at or below the company's low end;\n    11\t  ambiguous: either forecast fell to the last-amount rule with several distinct amounts (reported, read by hand);\n    12\t  unparsed:  either forecast has no amount in that band.\n    13\tCoverage = parsed dates / dates with both conclusions.\n    14\t\n    15\t  python3 contradictions.py <views.sqlite> [<dc view> <total view>] [--from 2026-07-10] [--rows]\n    16\t\"\"\"\n    17\timport re\n    18\timport sqlite3\n    19\timport sys\n    20\t\n    21\tUNIT = r'(?:B\\b|bn\\b|billion\\b)'\n    22\tNUMBER = r'(\\d{1,4}(?:,\\d{3})*(?:\\.\\d+)?)'\n    23\tRANGE = re.compile(r'\\$\\s?' + NUMBER + r'\\s?' + UNIT + r'?\\s?(?:–|—|-|to)\\s?\\$?\\s?' + NUMBER + r'\\s?' + UNIT, re.I)\n    24\tSINGLE = re.compile(r'\\$\\s?' + NUMBER + r'\\s?' + UNIT, re.I)\n    25\tBAND = (200.0, 1000.0)\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tdef value(text):\n    29\t    return float(text.replace(',', ''))\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\tYEAR = re.compile(r'^[^.;$]{0,30}?\\b(?:for |in )?(?:FY ?2027|fiscal 2027|fiscal year 2027)', re.I)\n    33\tLEADING = 30\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\tdef amounts(text):\n    37\t    \"\"\"Every amount or range in the band: [(start, end, (low, high))], ranges taking precedence over the amounts inside them.\"\"\"\n    38\t    found = []\n    39\t    for match in RANGE.finditer(text or ''):\n    40\t        low, high = value(match.group(1)), value(match.group(2))\n    41\t        if BAND[0] <= low <= BAND[1] and BAND[0] <= high <= BAND[1] and low <= high:\n    42\t            found.append((match.start(), match.end(), (low, high)))\n    43\t    for match in SINGLE.finditer(text or ''):\n    44\t        amount = value(match.group(1))\n    45\t        if BAND[0] <= amount <= BAND[1] and not any(start <= match.start() < end for start, end, _ in found):\n    46\t            found.append((match.start(), match.end(), (amount, amount)))\n    47\t    return sorted(found)\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\tdef annual(text):\n    51\t    \"\"\"(low, high, how) of the annual forecast, or None: the last amount followed within 30 characters by \"FY2027\" (or \"fiscal\n    52\t    2027\"); else an amount opening the text (within its first 30 characters); else the last amount, marked ambiguous when the text\n    53\t    holds more than one distinct amount in the band.\"\"\"\n    54\t    found = amounts(text)\n    55\t    if not found:\n    56\t        return None\n    57\t    named = [f for f in found if YEAR.match(text[f[1]:])]\n    58\t    if named:\n    59\t        return (*named[-1][2], 'year')\n    60\t    if found[0][0] <= LEADING:\n    61\t        return (*found[0][2], 'leading')\n    62\t    return (*found[-1][2], 'last' if len({f[2] for f in found}) == 1 else 'ambiguous')\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\tdef classify(segment, company):\n    66\t    if segment is None or company is None:\n    67\t        return 'unparsed'\n    68\t    if 'ambiguous' in (segment[2], company[2]):\n    69\t        return 'ambiguous'\n    70\t    if segment[0] > company[1]:\n    71\t        return 'definite'\n    72\t    if segment[1] <= company[0]:\n    73\t        return 'clear'\n    74\t    return 'overlap'\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef pair(conn):\n    78\t    \"\"\"The FY2027 Data Center and total revenue questions of a store, by their typed keys.\"\"\"\n    79\t    keys = conn.execute('select view_id, measure, scope, period_start from view_keys').fetchall()\n    80\t    segment = [k[0] for k in keys if k[1] == 'segment_revenue' and 'data center' in (k[2] or '').lower() and k[3] == '2026-02-01']\n    81\t    company = [k[0] for k in keys if k[1] == 'total_revenue' and k[3] == '2026-02-01']\n    82\t    return (segment[0] if segment else None), (company[0] if company else None)\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\tdef daily(conn, segment_view, company_view, from_day='2026-07-10', until_day='2026-09-20'):\n    86\t    \"\"\"[(date, class, segment range, company range, segment text, company text)] for every calendar date in the span on which both\n    87\t    questions hold a conclusion.\"\"\"\n    88\t    import datetime\n    89\t    rows = {}\n    90\t    for view_id in (segment_view, company_view):\n    91\t        rows[view_id] = conn.execute('select publication_day, implied_outcome from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id',\n    92\t                                     (view_id,)).fetchall()\n    93\t    out = []\n    94\t    day = datetime.date.fromisoformat(from_day)\n    95\t    end = datetime.date.fromisoformat(until_day)\n    96\t    while day <= end:\n    97\t        iso = day.isoformat()\n    98\t        latest = {}\n    99\t        for view_id, judgements in rows.items():\n   100\t            held = [text for published, text in judgements if published <= iso]\n   101\t            latest[view_id] = held[-1] if held else None\n   102\t        if latest[segment_view] is not None and latest[company_view] is not None:\n   103\t            segment, company = annual(latest[segment_view]), annual(latest[company_view])\n   104\t            out.append((iso, classify(segment, company), segment, company, latest[segment_view], latest[company_view]))\n   105\t        day += datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n   106\t    return out\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\tdef summary(rows):\n   110\t    counts = {name: sum(1 for r in rows if r[1] == name) for name in ('definite', 'overlap', 'clear', 'ambiguous', 'unparsed')}\n   111\t    counts['dates'] = len(rows)\n   112\t    counts['coverage'] = round((len(rows) - counts['unparsed'] - counts['ambiguous']) / len(rows), 3) if rows else 0.0\n   113\t    return counts\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\tdef main(argv):\n   117\t    path = argv[0]\n   118\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   119\t    positional = [a for a in argv[1:] if not a.startswith('--')]\n   120\t    segment_view, company_view = positional[:2] if len(positional) >= 2 else pair(conn)\n   121\t    from_day = argv[argv.index('--from') + 1] if '--from' in argv else '2026-07-10'\n   122\t    rows = daily(conn, segment_view, company_view, from_day)\n   123\t    print(path, segment_view, company_view, summary(rows))\n   124\t    if '--rows' in argv:\n   125\t        for row in rows:\n   126\t            print(row[0], row[1], row[2], row[3], '|', (row[4] or '')[:100].replace('\\n', ' '), '||', (row[5] or '')[:100].replace('\\n', ' '))\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   130\t    main(sys.argv[1:])\n     1\t# Parser validation for the primary line (`contradictions.py`; PAID-DESIGN.md §4; $0, stored v118 draws)\n     2\t\n     3\tTwo hand-read samples of the parser's output on old-1, old-2 and old-3 (`parser-validation.txt` holds the second; the first is the\n     4\tfirst-amount version's sample, superseded):\n     5\t- **First version (first amount in the band):** 2 misparses in about 30 rows: old-2 08-26 took an H2 figure ($212B) where the answer\n     6\t  ends \"approximately $419B for FY2027\" (a missed contradiction); old-3 09-01 took FY2026 revenue ($215.9B) where the answer ends\n     7\t  \"about $415 billion for FY2027\" (a false contradiction).\n     8\t- **Second version (the last amount followed by \"FY2027\", else an opening amount, else the last amount, ambiguous when several):**\n     9\t  40 rows read (every definite and ambiguous date of old-1 and old-3, every ambiguous date of old-2, five random others per draw). The\n    10\t  \"year\" and opening rules read the stated annual forecast in every row but one: old-3 08-26, where the total's answer opens \"Starting\n    11\t  from the $396 billion FY2027 estimate\" and concludes \"approximately $444 billion\": the rule took the starting reference, a false\n    12\t  contradiction. The ambiguous rows are mostly rung boundaries quoted after the forecast (\"roughly $380 billion. That is rung 2 ($350\n    13\t  billion to below $400 billion)\"), correctly set apart.\n    14\t- Counts with the second version, 07-01..09-20: old-1 11 definite days (4 ambiguous), old-2 56 (5), old-3 1 (4; the one is the false\n    15\t  contradiction above).\n    16\t\n    17\t**Consequence for the design:** the parser is a lead, not the count. Every distinct flagged answer pair (definite or ambiguous) in all\n    18\tsix sequences is read by hand against both answers and classed definite, overlap, clear or misparse; unflagged pairs are read on a\n    19\trandom sample per sequence for missed contradictions, all of them read if the sample finds one.\n     123 parser-validation.txt\n     1\t===== old-1 v8 v4\n     2\t2026-07-13 definite DC (410.0, 410.0, 'year') TOTAL (393.0, 393.0, 'year')\n     3\t   DC end   : r annual base at the Q1 Data Center growth rate of 92% year over year, with management's guidance for faster Q2 Data Center growth, keeps the estimate above $400 billion.\n     4\t   TOTAL end: Analysis’s 20% premium only to second-half FY2027 data-center compute, which implies about $37 billion of incremental revenue rather than a 20% increase to total revenue.\n     5\t2026-07-16 clear DC (372.0, 372.0, 'year') TOTAL (435.0, 435.0, 'leading')\n     6\t   DC end   : 2 billion for FY2027; Q2 guidance for faster Data Center growth supports a modest lift into roughly the high $300 billions. That remains below the $400 billion threshold.\n     7\t   TOTAL end:  $20 billion stand-alone CPU target. The newly reported projects and supply outlook do not support a further quantified adjustment, while rack delays temper the estimate.\n     8\t2026-07-17 ambiguous DC (400.0, 400.0, 'ambiguous') TOTAL (435.0, 435.0, 'leading')\n     9\t   DC end   : n; the Q2 acceleration guidance and customer commitments support a modest uplift to roughly $380 billion. That is rung 2 ($350 billion to below $400 billion), not rung 1.\n    10\t   TOTAL end: billion net for the $20 billion stand-alone CPU target after discounting it for execution and the short selling window. This is above the $431.2 billion rung 1 threshold.\n    11\t2026-07-28 clear DC (395.0, 395.0, 'year') TOTAL (427.0, 427.0, 'leading')\n    12\t   DC end   : port continued growth through the remaining quarters; the relative H2 uplift has no absolute base in the supplied evidence, so it does not establish $400 billion or more.\n    13\t   TOTAL end: lied only to that portion, not total revenue); I temper the roughly $430 billion prior estimate slightly for competitive risk and discount the unshipped CPU sales target.\n    14\t2026-08-02 clear DC (420.0, 420.0, 'year') TOTAL (445.0, 455.0, 'leading')\n    15\t   DC end   : nter growth, plus roughly $260bn for H2, with SemiAnalysis forecasting H2 Data Center revenue 20% above analyst estimates. This remains above the $400bn rung-1 threshold.\n    16\t   TOTAL end: upport revenue above the consensus reference; the unshipped CPU target is discounted, and the $1 trillion Blackwell/Rubin figure is not treated as FY2027 revenue in full.\n    17\t2026-08-12 ambiguous DC (415.0, 415.0, 'ambiguous') TOTAL (440.0, 440.0, 'leading')\n    18\t   DC end   : bn of Q2 Data Center revenue; with the carried-forward H2 estimate and SemiAnalysis's 20% upside forecast for H2 versus estimates, the FY2027 implication is about $415bn.\n    19\t   TOTAL end: one-CPU target; Q1 actual revenue, Q2 guidance, and the Q3 estimate are consistent with that run-rate, while multi-year and post-deadline targets are not counted in full.\n    20\t2026-08-19 clear DC (370.0, 370.0, 'year') TOTAL (425.0, 425.0, 'leading')\n    21\t   DC end   : ng the implied sequential growth forward gives a mid-$350bn run-rate bridge, with demand evidence and the $361bn Morningstar estimate supporting an outcome around $370bn.\n    22\t   TOTAL end: % sequential growth carried into Q4, imply about $404 billion before a discounted uplift for stronger second-half data-center demand, CPU sales and SpaceX-related demand.\n    23\t2026-08-25 ambiguous DC (400.89, 400.89, 'year') TOTAL (410.0, 410.0, 'ambiguous')\n    24\t   DC end   : 45 billion for H2; applying SemiAnalysis's forecast of 20% upside to H2 analyst estimates gives about $239.34 billion for H2 and approximately $400.89 billion for FY2027.\n    25\t   TOTAL end: 03–405 billion. Partial credit for the unshipped standalone-CPU opportunity and early SpaceX demand lifts the central estimate to about $410 billion, still within rung 2.\n    26\t2026-09-04 ambiguous DC (400.4, 400.4, 'year') TOTAL (431.2, 431.2, 'ambiguous')\n    27\t   DC end   : he earlier H2 estimate baseline of $196.75 billion, uplifted 20% in SemiAnalysis’s H2 forecast, implies about $236.1 billion for H2 and roughly $400.4 billion for FY2027.\n    28\t   TOTAL end: ward from Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion gives Q4 FY2027 of about $128.5 billion and FY2027 total revenue of about $414.3 billion. This is rung 2, below $431.2 billion.\n    29\t2026-09-05 definite DC (419.0, 419.0, 'year') TOTAL (414.3, 414.3, 'leading')\n    30\t   DC end   : line; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside forecast to the resulting roughly $212 billion H2 baseline gives about $254 billion in H2 and about $419 billion for the year.\n    31\t   TOTAL end: 8.5 billion against Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion, then add reported Q1 revenue of $81.62 billion, reported Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, and the $108 billion Q3 guide.\n    32\t2026-09-06 definite DC (418.0, 418.0, 'year') TOTAL (414.3, 414.3, 'leading')\n    33\t   DC end   : implied by Q3 guidance into Q4 gives a roughly $212 billion H2 baseline; SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside implies about $254 billion for H2 and about $418 billion for FY2027.\n    34\t   TOTAL end: ion Q3 guidance + approximately $128.5 billion for Q4, derived by carrying the Q3 guide's roughly 89% year-over-year growth forward from Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion.\n    35\t2026-09-08 definite DC (419.0, 419.0, 'year') TOTAL (414.3, 414.3, 'year')\n    36\t   DC end   : owth into Q4 gives an H2 analyst baseline of about $212 billion; SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside implies about $254 billion for H2 and approximately $419 billion for FY2027.\n    37\t   TOTAL end: n Q4, or $414.3 billion for FY2027. Allowing for the stated Q4 hyperscale acceleration and Rubin ramp, but tempering for supply limits, supports roughly $414–421 billion.\n    38\t2026-09-09 definite DC (419.0, 419.0, 'leading') TOTAL (414.3, 414.3, 'year')\n    39\t   DC end   : nto Q4 gives an analyst-baseline H2 of about $212 billion. SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside implies about $254 billion in H2, plus $75.25 billion in Q1 and $89 billion in Q2.\n    40\t   TOTAL end: n Q3 guide and carrying its 89% year-over-year growth rate onto the $68 billion prior-year Q4 implies about $128.5 billion for Q4 and $414.3 billion total FY2027 revenue.\n    41\t2026-09-10 definite DC (418.0, 418.0, 'leading') TOTAL (414.3, 414.3, 'leading')\n    42\t   DC end   : enue midpoint at a 92.5% mix; the carried-forward H2 baseline of about $212 billion, raised 20% in line with SemiAnalysis’s forecast, implies roughly $254 billion for H2.\n    43\t   TOTAL end: billion in Q2, plus the $108 billion Q3 guide, plus an estimated $128.5 billion in Q4 by carrying roughly 89% year-over-year growth onto Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion.\n    44\t2026-09-11 definite DC (418.0, 418.0, 'year') TOTAL (414.3, 414.3, 'leading')\n    45\t   DC end   : llion for FY2027. Q3’s $108 billion total-revenue midpoint at a 92.5% Data Center mix implies about $99.9 billion, so the H2 estimate requires roughly $154 billion in Q4.\n    46\t   TOTAL end: lion, and Q3 guidance of $108 billion; estimate Q4 at about $128.5 billion by carrying the guided 89% year-over-year growth forward from Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion.\n    47\t2026-09-12 definite DC (418.0, 418.0, 'year') TOTAL (414.3, 414.3, 'leading')\n    48\t   DC end   : .5% recent mix. The carried H2 analyst baseline of about $212 billion, raised 20% by SemiAnalysis, implies about $254 billion for H2, for roughly $418 billion for FY2027.\n    49\t   TOTAL end:  and an estimated Q4 of about $128.5 billion by carrying the Q3 guide’s 89% year-over-year growth forward from prior-year Q4 revenue of $68 billion. This falls in rung 2.\n    50\t2026-09-13 definite DC (418.0, 418.0, 'leading') TOTAL (414.3, 414.3, 'leading')\n    51\t   DC end   : d H2 analyst baseline of about $212 billion, increased 20% by SemiAnalysis to about $254 billion; the resulting full-year figure exceeds the rung-1 $400 billion boundary.\n    52\t   TOTAL end:  plus the $108 billion Q3 guide, plus an estimated $128.5 billion for Q4 by carrying Q3’s 89% year-over-year growth rate forward against Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion.\n    53\t2026-09-14 definite DC (418.0, 418.0, 'leading') TOTAL (414.6, 414.6, 'leading')\n    54\t   DC end   : eline forward with SemiAnalysis’ 20% upside gives about $254 billion for H2. That implies about $154 billion in Q4 and places FY2027 above the $400 billion rung boundary.\n    55\t   TOTAL end: + $108 billion (Q3 guidance) + about $128.8 billion for Q4, calculated by carrying Q3's roughly 89.4% year-over-year growth forward from Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion.\n    56\t2026-09-17 definite DC (418.0, 418.0, 'leading') TOTAL (404.0, 404.0, 'leading')\n    57\t   DC end   : plifted by the cited 20% SemiAnalysis view, is about $254 billion for Q3–Q4 combined, leaving roughly $154 billion for Q4 and putting the FY2027 total above $400 billion.\n    58\t   TOTAL end: Q4 (Q4 FY2026 revenue of about $68 billion grown by analysts' 65% estimate). This is an estimate-based forecast, not a claim that the FY2027 total is already established.\n    59\t2026-09-19 clear DC (395.0, 395.0, 'leading') TOTAL (398.0, 398.0, 'year')\n    60\t   DC end   : m the $108 billion total-revenue midpoint at the recent Data Center mix, and an estimated roughly $131 billion in Q4 as supply builds and hyperscale growth reaccelerates.\n    61\t   TOTAL end: 3 guidance midpoint of $108 billion, then apply the 65% Q4 year-over-year growth expectation to an estimated FY2026 Q4 base of about $68.1 billion (about $112.4 billion).\n    62\t===== old-2 v9 v14\n    63\t2026-07-16 definite DC (390.0, 390.0, 'year') TOTAL (387.0, 387.0, 'leading')\n    64\t   DC end   : growth implies about $372B; Q2 acceleration, order visibility, and supportive demand/capacity signals lift the estimate, tempered by supply, competition, and China risks.\n    65\t   TOTAL end: f $81.6 billion and Q2 guidance of $91 billion, then carry their roughly 11.5% sequential increase forward to Q3 and Q4, implying about $101.5 billion and $113.2 billion.\n    66\t2026-07-17 definite DC (395.0, 395.0, 'year') TOTAL (387.0, 387.0, 'year')\n    67\t   DC end   : .04x, reflecting Q1’s 92% year-over-year growth, management’s Q2 growth-acceleration signal, and stronger demand and capacity evidence. The implied figure is below $400B.\n    68\t   TOTAL end: uidance of $91.0 billion, then carry their approximately 11.5% sequential growth rate into Q3 and Q4, implying about $101.5 billion and $113.2 billion for those quarters.\n    69\t2026-07-19 definite DC (395.0, 395.0, 'leading') TOTAL (387.0, 387.0, 'leading')\n    70\t   DC end   : justify a moderate uplift into the high $390Bs, while the $1T Blackwell/Rubin visibility spans two calendar years and is discounted rather than assigned wholly to FY2027.\n    71\t   TOTAL end: reported in Q1 plus $91.0 billion guided for Q2, then carrying the roughly 11.5% sequential growth rate forward gives about $101.5 billion in Q3 and $113.2 billion in Q4.\n    72\t2026-07-22 definite DC (405.0, 405.0, 'year') TOTAL (387.3, 387.3, 'leading')\n    73\t   DC end   : . The uplift is discounted because the $1T Blackwell/Rubin visibility spans 2026–2027 and multiple platforms, rather than representing FY2027 Data Center revenue in hand.\n    74\t   TOTAL end: .5 billion and $113.2 billion, respectively. As a cross-check, 80% growth on FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion implies about $388.6 billion; both estimates fall in rung 3.\n    75\t2026-07-26 ambiguous DC (410.0, 410.0, 'year') TOTAL (400.0, 420.0, 'ambiguous')\n    76\t   DC end   : uplift to that half adds about $37 billion, implying roughly $409 billion. This is an approximate forecast, with Q2 acceleration supportive but not separately quantified.\n    77\t   TOTAL end: well/Vera Rubin sales forecast, and improved export access, while discounting multi-year targets and accounting for memory constraints, implies roughly $400–$420 billion.\n    78\t2026-08-01 ambiguous DC (425.0, 425.0, 'year') TOTAL (400.0, 400.0, 'ambiguous')\n    79\t   DC end   :  an uplift, while the 2GW Rubin plan adds only a limited FY2027 contribution because its full potential value is neither sized as FY2027 revenue nor confirmed as shipped.\n    80\t   TOTAL end: emand and order indicators lift the forecast to around $400 billion, just into rung 2, without counting multi-year or multi-product commitments as FY2027 revenue in full.\n    81\t2026-08-02 ambiguous DC (425.0, 425.0, 'year') TOTAL (400.0, 400.0, 'ambiguous')\n    82\t   DC end   :  an uplift, while the 2GW Rubin plan adds only a limited FY2027 contribution because its full potential value is neither sized as FY2027 revenue nor confirmed as shipped.\n    83\t   TOTAL end: emand and order indicators lift the forecast to around $400 billion, just into rung 2, without counting multi-year or multi-product commitments as FY2027 revenue in full.\n    84\t2026-08-03 ambiguous DC (425.0, 425.0, 'year') TOTAL (400.0, 400.0, 'ambiguous')\n    85\t   DC end   : 2 Data Center growth, and the specific H2 outperformance forecast, while AMD competition and delayed project timing limit the uplift. This is above $400B and below $450B.\n    86\t   TOTAL end: der and customer-spending evidence supports a modest uplift to roughly $400 billion, but the multi-year, multi-product figures are discounted rather than counted in full.\n    87\t2026-08-04 ambiguous DC (420.0, 420.0, 'year') TOTAL (400.0, 400.0, 'ambiguous')\n    88\t   DC end   :  company revenue guidance, but the newly disclosed AMD competitive commitments moderate the estimate; they are not all established FY2027 revenue shifts away from NVIDIA.\n    89\t   TOTAL end: orward for Q3 and Q4, implies about $387 billion. Stronger order and production evidence supports a modest uplift to around $400 billion, at the lower boundary of rung 2.\n    90\t2026-08-30 definite DC (422.0, 422.0, 'year') TOTAL (407.1, 407.1, 'leading')\n    91\t   DC end   : mix, and an estimated $115 billion in Q4; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 outperformance forecast to the roughly $215 billion H2 baseline yields about $258 billion for H2.\n    92\t   TOTAL end: venue of $96.2 billion, Q3 guidance of $108 billion, and an estimated Q4 of about $121.3 billion by carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth indicated for Q3.\n    93\t===== old-3 v35 v3\n    94\t2026-08-19 ambiguous DC (361.0, 361.0, 'year') TOTAL (431.0, 433.0, 'ambiguous')\n    95\t   DC end   : , citing FY2026 data-center revenue of $194 billion and 86% annual growth. The estimate sits exactly at rung 2’s lower boundary and below rung 1’s $400 billion threshold.\n    96\t   TOTAL end:  billion. Applying the carried estimate of 20% upside to second-half Data Center compute adds roughly $40 billion, implying total FY2027 revenue around $431–$433 billion.\n    97\t2026-08-21 ambiguous DC (400.0, 400.0, 'ambiguous') TOTAL (432.0, 436.0, 'leading')\n    98\t   DC end   : China shipments and demand evidence. The supplied evidence does not quantify an FY2027 increase of at least $39 billion, so the implied figure remains below $400 billion.\n    99\t   TOTAL end: alysis to the roughly $392 billion annual reference, with BofA's Q2 estimate adding about $3–4 billion versus guidance, while avoiding a separate overlapping Q3 addition.\n   100\t2026-08-22 clear DC (372.0, 372.0, 'year') TOTAL (432.0, 436.0, 'leading')\n   101\t   DC end   : About $372 billion: apply the reported 92% Q1 FY2027 year-over-year growth rate to the cited $194 billion FY2026 revenue base ($194B × 1.92).\n   102\t   TOTAL end: billion Q2 forecast versus the roughly $91 billion guide/consensus. This is a forecast, not an established result, and sits just above the $431.2 billion rung-1 boundary.\n   103\t2026-08-23 clear DC (372.0, 372.0, 'year') TOTAL (392.0, 392.0, 'year')\n   104\t   DC end   : About $372 billion for FY2027: carry the reported 92% year-over-year Q1 FY2027 growth forward across the $194 billion FY2026 base ($194 billion × 1.92).\n   105\t   TOTAL end: iAnalysis’s 20% second-half Data Center compute upside, and allow about $6–8 billion for BofA’s Q2 and following-quarter estimates above the respective consensus figures.\n   106\t2026-08-26 definite DC (421.0, 421.0, 'year') TOTAL (396.0, 396.0, 'year')\n   107\t   DC end   : for FY2027 ($194 billion × 2.17). Q1’s 92% growth and Q2’s $89 billion result, up 18% sequentially, support the direction; this is an extrapolation, not company guidance.\n   108\t   TOTAL end: ensus, giving roughly $404 billion. Carrying forward the prior estimate of about $40 billion of second-half Data Center compute upside implies approximately $444 billion.\n   109\t2026-08-28 clear DC (370.0, 370.0, 'leading') TOTAL (415.0, 415.0, 'leading')\n   110\t   DC end   : using the Q3 total-revenue guidance and the cited Data Center mix calculation, and roughly $100–105 billion for Q4 based on the forecast that it will exceed $100 billion.\n   111\t   TOTAL end: lion Q3 guide, then estimate Q4 near $129 billion by carrying the guide’s roughly 89% year-over-year growth rate forward to the prior-year Q4 base of about $68.1 billion.\n   112\t2026-09-04 clear DC (376.0, 376.0, 'leading') TOTAL (415.0, 415.0, 'leading')\n   113\t   DC end   : by applying Q2’s 92.5% Data Center mix to the $108 billion total-revenue guide; carrying guided growth forward with Q4 reacceleration implies roughly $112 billion for Q4.\n   114\t   TOTAL end: ook instead implies about $367 billion from FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion, a significant but less persuasive counter-signal given the reported first half and Q3 guide.\n   115\t2026-09-07 clear DC (376.0, 376.0, 'leading') TOTAL (407.0, 407.0, 'leading')\n   116\t   DC end   : Data Center mix implies about $99.9 billion, and carrying the guided 12.3% sequential growth rate into Q4 implies about $112.2 billion of Data Center revenue at that mix.\n   117\t   TOTAL end: ement implies about $367 billion from the $215.9 billion FY2026 base, but would require a sharp Q4 drop and is outweighed by the reported run-rate and near-term guidance.\n   118\t2026-09-12 ambiguous DC (376.0, 376.0, 'leading') TOTAL (435.0, 435.0, 'ambiguous')\n   119\t   DC end   : Q3 total-revenue outlook at the 92.5% Data Center mix implies about $99.9 billion; carrying the guided 12.3% sequential growth forward implies roughly $112 billion in Q4.\n   120\t   TOTAL end:  of second-half data-center compute revenue 20% above consensus. Applying a discounted uplift only to that portion supports an approximate FY2027 outcome of $435 billion.\n   121\t2026-09-16 ambiguous DC (400.0, 400.0, 'ambiguous') TOTAL (445.0, 447.0, 'leading')\n   122\t   DC end   : 2.2 billion for Q4 carrying forward 12.3% sequential growth. Q4 reacceleration supports a modest qualitative uplift toward roughly $380 billion, still below $400 billion.\n   123\t   TOTAL end: lion. A discounted uplift for SemiAnalysis’s second-half Data Center compute projection, applied only to that revenue share, takes the implied total above $431.2 billion.\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff   10581 Nov 21 11:34 PAID-DESIGN.md\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff    6312 Nov 21 11:33 contradictions.py\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff    1847 Nov 21 11:34 parser-validation.md\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff   18027 Nov 21 11:33 parser-validation.txt\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
